The geodata are not. Everything under data/, and everything the build
derives from it (public/data/, the tilesets), comes from third-party open
data and stays under the licence of its source:

  - State geodata (DGM1, DOM1, LoD2, Basis-DLM, DOP, laser scans), one
    provider per Land (sites/providers.ts):
      Quelle: GeoSN, dl-de/by-2-0
      Freie und Hansestadt Hamburg, Landesbetrieb Geoinformation und
        Vermessung (LGV), dl-de/by-2-0
      Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung – www.geodaten.bayern.de, CC BY 4.0
      Geobasis NRW, dl-de/zero-2-0
      Geoportal Berlin, dl-de/zero-2-0

  - OpenStreetMap: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License
    (ODbL) 1.0. The layers derived from it are databases under the ODbL,
    share-alike included: a database derived from them stays under the
    ODbL.

  - Wikidata: CC0 1.0.

  - The walks' photos (data/<site>/walks/photos/): Wikimedia Commons
    files, each under the licence its Commons page states and credited
    with its author, licence and page in the walk's file (photo) and on
    the stop's card. Reduced to 800 px and re-encoded as WebP.

  - The cities' and Länder's street-tree cadastres, traffic counts and
    cycle counters: dl-de/by-2-0 or dl-de/zero-2-0, credited to the city
    or Land that publishes them.

  - GTFS timetable: DELFI e.V. via gtfs.de, CC BY 4.0.

  - Copernicus DEM GLO-30 (the land beyond each site, in the baked sky
    view and horizon, data/<site>/dlm/svf_* and horizon_*): produced using
    Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and
    Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union
    and ESA; all rights reserved. The organisations in charge of the
    Copernicus programme by law or by delegation do not incur any
    liability for any use of the Copernicus WorldDEM-30.

  - Mapillary's detected objects (the street lamps OpenStreetMap lacks in
    Dresden, Grimma, Meißen and Unna, data/<site>/dlm/mly_*.geojson):
    Mapillary, CC BY-SA 4.0. Kept in their own files, apart from the ODbL
    layers.

  - The Deutscher Wetterdienst's phenology reporters (the trees' leaf-out,
    autumn and leaf-fall days and each city's shift from Dresden's, read
    into lib/city/tree-season.ts): Quelle: Deutscher Wetterdienst,
    dl-de/by-2-0.

Every source with its licence and required credit is listed in
docs/guide/en/data-sources.md, section "Licences and credits" (in German:
docs/guide/de/data-sources.md, "Lizenzen und Quellenvermerke").
